            "type": "game",
            "name": "The Great Wobo Escape",
            "steam_appid": 564480,
            "required_age": 0,
            "is_free": false,
            "detailed_description": "<h1>Características</h1><p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >FAMILY FRIENDLY FUN</h2>Approachable by young audience – no blood, just a comic mischief with a pinch of sabotage towards evil robots!<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >STEALTH &amp; ACTION</h2>Fast-paced action-filled stealth game full of puzzles, deadly enemies, hidden passages, dangerous traps and tricky hazards.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >BEAUTIFUL 3D GRAPHICS</h2>Play a game full of small details, featuring high-res textures, detailed environments and distinctive characters. Configure additional effects (depth of field, anisotropic filtering, specular highlights, postprocess effects) for even more immersive atmosphere.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >VISUALLY UNIQUE</h2>Unique visual style – play as a futuristic high-tech robot, fight dieselpunk enemies of various sizes and shapes.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >SCI-FI STORY</h2>Rich story in an absorbing sci-fi world exploring a thin line between a machine and a living intelligence, where colony’s AI went rogue and persecutes other robots.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >CONTROLLER SUPPORT</h2>Play comfortably with your controller (most controllers supported)!</p><br><h1>Known Issues</h1><p>Here is a list of known issues:<br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Game crashes immediately after launch when MSI After Burner software is also running<br></li><li>Controller is recognized and ready to use only if it is connected (or re-connected) after game's launch</li></ul></p><br><h1>Acerca do jogo</h1>Main character in The Great Wobo Escape is robot named Wobo. He is alone, unarmed, and escaping for freedom, his only chance is to hide in shadows, use the environment to his favor and crush dieselpunk enemy robots. Stealth approach may quickly shift into fast-paced escape combined with creating diversion, causing chaos and avoiding tricky hazards.<br><br>The Great Wobo Escape combines stealth with action-oriented gameplay and a subtle sci-fi story (How much intelligent must robots become to deserve freedom?). Game is approachable by young audience.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Cloud Saves &amp; Progress</h2>Unfortunately, we do not support cloud saves - please note this as you delete the game, your stats and collectibles will be lost. <br>All 8 levels are available from the start. You are free to play them in any order you want... although we suggest to go from 1st to the last ;)<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Controls</h2>This game features support for mouse &amp; keyboard as well as full controller support. Each control type has two options - a common layouts. Controls are not configurable.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Graphics, Performance &amp; Screenshots</h2>All screenshots represent typical gameplay, were take in Full HD (native 1920x1080) using in-game settings and were not enhanced or altered in any way. Game has been tested to perform 60+ FPS in 4k with Intel i7 7700k @ 4.5GHz, GTX 970 (MSI), 16GB DDR4 RAM (just for a reference).<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Czech language</h2>Czech subtitles for all dialogues and for all texts is available through Options &gt; Gameplay (Nastavení &gt; Hratelnost) from the main menu.",
            "about_the_game": "Main character in The Great Wobo Escape is robot named Wobo. He is alone, unarmed, and escaping for freedom, his only chance is to hide in shadows, use the environment to his favor and crush dieselpunk enemy robots. Stealth approach may quickly shift into fast-paced escape combined with creating diversion, causing chaos and avoiding tricky hazards.<br><br>The Great Wobo Escape combines stealth with action-oriented gameplay and a subtle sci-fi story (How much intelligent must robots become to deserve freedom?). Game is approachable by young audience.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Cloud Saves &amp; Progress</h2>Unfortunately, we do not support cloud saves - please note this as you delete the game, your stats and collectibles will be lost. <br>All 8 levels are available from the start. You are free to play them in any order you want... although we suggest to go from 1st to the last ;)<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Controls</h2>This game features support for mouse &amp; keyboard as well as full controller support. Each control type has two options - a common layouts. Controls are not configurable.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Graphics, Performance &amp; Screenshots</h2>All screenshots represent typical gameplay, were take in Full HD (native 1920x1080) using in-game settings and were not enhanced or altered in any way. Game has been tested to perform 60+ FPS in 4k with Intel i7 7700k @ 4.5GHz, GTX 970 (MSI), 16GB DDR4 RAM (just for a reference).<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Czech language</h2>Czech subtitles for all dialogues and for all texts is available through Options &gt; Gameplay (Nastavení &gt; Hratelnost) from the main menu.",
            "short_description": "In The Great Wobo Escape, you must help the high-tech robot Wobo escape from his mining colony. Guide him through a number of different levels using stealth, solving puzzles, and using the environment to avoid detection by dieselpunk robot overlords.",
            "supported_languages": "Inglês, Checo",
